<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mpu Sindok</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/929">929</a>–<a href="/years/947">947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mpu Sindok was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medang-kingdom">Medang</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> who moved the royal centre from Central to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a> around 929, possibly after eruptions of Merapi or pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a>. He founded the Isyana dynasty, and some twenty inscriptions survive from his reign, which lasted until about 947. Eastern Java remained the centre of Javanese kingship for the following centuries.</p></div>
